findings.evidence:
storage/registry.rs persists domain types directly:
- `Vec<crate::domain::action_shortcut::ActionBinding>` (48);
- `Vec<crate::domain::operator_action::OperatorPin>` (51);
- `Vec<crate::domain::health::AudioRule>` (54);
- `deserialize_with = "crate::domain::audio_preset::deserialize_presets"` (58).

The domain carries file-format attributes: deny_unknown_fields, `try_from = "f64"` (audio_preset.rs:15), and the private `#[serde(default, rename = "path", skip_serializing)] legacy_path` (appearance.rs:288-289). A domain test builds crate::storage::registry::SceneRegistry (audio_preset.rs:102).

Validation is a separate call on structs with public fields:
- AudioPreset{pub inputs} with a separate valid() (58-77);
- PresetPlan::valid reads the clock via `self.reviewed.elapsed() <= 30s` (run.rs:25);
- ActionShortcut::valid (action_shortcut.rs:33-52) works on a bare String key.

The two name rules differ: bookmark::valid_name trims, max 120 (bookmark.rs:39-43), while audio_preset::valid_name rejects surrounding whitespace, max 80 (51-56). controller/state/bookmarks.rs:59 trims bookmark names before storing them.

OBS protocol facts in the domain:
- is_text_kind lists OBS kind ids (control.rs:288-297) and is used only by obs/client.rs:652,967;
- tracks: [bool; 6] (control.rs:203);
- ChannelLevel::from_mul([f32;3]) and InputLevels::from_mul (meter.rs:89-97,127-139) encode the obs-websocket meter wire shape;
- PresetInput::same_values casts to f32 (run.rs:39-46).

findings.verifier_note:
Verified:
- 22 variants, from SetItemEnabled to SetAudioTracks;
- `impl ControlAction` at 14-22 precedes the declaration at 221;
- 18 files reference the enum.

ControlAction derives only Debug, Clone and PartialEq (no serde), so nesting does not affect any persisted format. The rename to AudioMonitoring is justified: health::audio::AudioMonitor exists with the same name.

The reviewer's failure scenario (stale index puts the wrong name in session reports) is not supported by the code:
- collect_report recomputes `self.health.alerts(now)` every tick and resolves `self.health.audio.name(index)` against the same watches vector immediately (session_reports.rs:336-352);
- the report stores the resolved name string;
- a rule change rebuilds watches and their Sustained state together (health/audio.rs:67-72), so no alert survives with an old index;
- ui/health_alerts.rs:28-46 also resolves at render from the same monitor;
- audio alerts have event_id None, so acknowledge (events.rs:121-125) is a no-op for them.

